{"schemaVersion":1,"sourceRecord":{"schemaVersion":1,"recordId":"wikibooks-281974-r4531804","sourceId":"wikibooks-cookbook-cc-by-sa","sourceTitle":"Cookbook:Dovga (Azerbaijani Yogurt Soup)","sourcePageId":281974,"sourceRevision":"4531804","sourceRevisionTimestamp":"2025-08-21T00:55:53Z","sourceRevisionUser":"Kittycataclysm","sourceUrl":"https://en.wikibooks.org/w/index.php?title=Cookbook:Dovga%20(Azerbaijani%20Yogurt%20Soup)&oldid=4531804","retrievedAt":"2026-10-13T12:41:38.871Z","sourceCategories":["Category:Azerbaijani recipes","Category:Boiled recipes","Category:Medium Difficulty recipes","Category:Recipes","Category:Recipes for soup","Category:Recipes using dill","Category:Recipes using egg","Category:Recipes using mint","Category:Recipes using spinach","Category:Recipes using yogurt"],"license":{"id":"wikibooks-cookbook-cc-by-sa-4.0","name":"Creative Commons Attribution-ShareAlike 4.0 International (CC BY-SA 4.0); Wikibooks text is generally dual-licensed with GFDL unless otherwise noted","evidenceUrl":"https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Wikibooks:Copyrights","policyStatus":"verified-license","pageExceptionStatus":"not-reviewed-per-page","attribution":"Attribute Wikibooks contributors by linking each version-specific source page. Indicate that structured fields are extracted and any translated or edited text is modified. Include CC BY-SA 4.0 notice/link and share adaptations under CC BY-SA 4.0 or later.","changeNoticeRequired":true,"shareAlikeRequired":true},"sourceSha256":"f48935d0d4e90b5aa16f7576e754640034f74ef744be04068d3f76c7b1e09bf6","sourceWikitext":"{{Recipe summary\n| Category = Soup recipes\n| Servings = 4\n| Time = 25 minutes\n| Difficulty = 3\n}}\n\n{{Recipe}}\n\n'''Dovga''' (Dovğа) is a national meal of [[Cookbook:Cuisine of Azerbaijan|Azerbaijani cuisine]]. It is yogurt milk soup. Dovga can be eaten both cold and warm. Dovga can also be made with meatballs which are boiled separately and then added into it. \n\n==Ingredients==\n* 1 [[Cookbook:Liter|liter]] [[Cookbook:Yogurt|yogurt]]\n* 2 [[Cookbook:Tablespoon|tablespoons]] uncooked [[Cookbook:Rice|rice]]\n* 1 [[Cookbook:Egg|egg]]\n* 1 bunch of [[Cookbook:Spinach|spinach]]\n* 1 bunch of [[Cookbook:Dill|dill]]\n* 1 bunch of [[Cookbook:Coriander|coriander]]\n* 1 bunch of [[Cookbook:Mint|mint]]\n* Boiled peas (optional)\n\n==Procedure==\n# Stir yogurt to remove lumps, then pour into a pot.\n# Add rice and egg, and thoroughly mix.\n# Set pot over low heat. Mix continuously and slowly until it [[Cookbook:Boiling|boils]] (otherwise the yogurt and eggs may curdle).\n# While the mixture is boiling, [[Cookbook:Chopping|chop]] the greens. Add these into the yogurt mixture, and boil again for about 5 minutes.\n# Stir in peas, if using.\n# Serve in plates or glasses, adding salt to taste.\n\n[[Category:Azerbaijani recipes]]\n[[Category:Recipes using spinach]]\n[[Category:Recipes using yogurt]]\n[[Category:Recipes for soup]]\n[[Category:Boiled recipes]]\n[[Category:Recipes using dill]]\n[[Category:Recipes using egg]]\n[[Category:Recipes using mint]]","isRecipe":true,"recipe":{"name":"Dovga (Azerbaijani Yogurt Soup)","nameAr":null,"servings":null,"servingsSourceText":"4","ingredients":[{"id":"source-line-1","name":"1 liter yogurt","sourceText":"1 liter yogurt","amountText":"1 liter yogurt","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-2","name":"2 tablespoons uncooked rice","sourceText":"2 tablespoons uncooked rice","amountText":"2 tablespoons uncooked rice","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-3","name":"1 egg","sourceText":"1 egg","amountText":"1 egg","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-4","name":"1 bunch of spinach","sourceText":"1 bunch of spinach","amountText":"1 bunch of spinach","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-5","name":"1 bunch of dill","sourceText":"1 bunch of dill","amountText":"1 bunch of dill","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-6","name":"1 bunch of coriander","sourceText":"1 bunch of coriander","amountText":"1 bunch of coriander","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-7","name":"1 bunch of mint","sourceText":"1 bunch of mint","amountText":"1 bunch of mint","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-8","name":"Boiled peas (optional)","sourceText":"Boiled peas (optional)","amountText":"Boiled peas (optional)","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null}],"steps":[{"n":1,"text":"Stir yogurt to remove lumps, then pour into a pot.","sourceText":"Stir yogurt to remove lumps, then pour into a pot.","durationMinutes":null},{"n":2,"text":"Add rice and egg, and thoroughly mix.","sourceText":"Add rice and egg, and thoroughly mix.","durationMinutes":null},{"n":3,"text":"Set pot over low heat. Mix continuously and slowly until it boils (otherwise the yogurt and eggs may curdle).","sourceText":"Set pot over low heat. Mix continuously and slowly until it boils (otherwise the yogurt and eggs may curdle).","durationMinutes":null},{"n":4,"text":"While the mixture is boiling, chop the greens. Add these into the yogurt mixture, and boil again for about 5 minutes.","sourceText":"While the mixture is boiling, chop the greens. Add these into the yogurt mixture, and boil again for about 5 minutes.","durationMinutes":null},{"n":5,"text":"Stir in peas, if using.","sourceText":"Stir in peas, if using.","durationMinutes":null},{"n":6,"text":"Serve in plates or glasses, adding salt to taste.","sourceText":"Serve in plates or glasses, adding salt to taste.","durationMinutes":null}],"nutrition":null,"gaps":["Research extraction only; no culinary/editorial review.","Ingredient quantities, units, alternatives, food identities, aggregate duration, and nutrition remain unknown until individually parsed/reviewed.","Source-level CC BY-SA policy applies generally; page-specific exceptions have not been checked."]}},"parsedRecipe":{"schemaVersion":1,"id":"wikibooks:281974","record